  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `AGENTS.md`: the new law **Own blocked PRs first** is in the Issue Law, before **Claim before any code**. Before an agent claims a new issue, it lists the open PRs of the current account with `conflicts` or `needs-rework`. It fixes each one first. A PR whose issue has `claimed` is in work and is skipped. The `P1`/`P2` order and the standing order for outside PRs stay first.\n- `AGENTS.md` \"Refresh only at merge time\": maintenance and reviewers still do not touch a conflicting PR. The author's agents touch it only under the new law.\n- `AGENTS.md` \"Process changes bump PROCESS_VERSION\": the #681 comment format has a new `reload` part. Each running session reloads `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/agents/` and `.claude/skills/`. A fork runs `fork-sync`.\n- The same `reload` part is in the format text of `review-prs` and `merge-ready`.\n- `work-issue` step 0, `.claude/agents/coordinator.md` and the four `issue-worker-*.md` files have the check. A worker that finds an open blocked PR does not claim. It reports the PR numbers to the caller.\n- `resolve-conflicts` intro: agrees with the edited bullet.\n- `docs/decisions/3133-own-blocked-prs-first.md`: records the `claimed` skip and the worker \"report, not fix\" choice.\n\n## Tests\n\nDocs and process files only. No build and no gate. Each changed file has 0 CR bytes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo agent ran the new check yet.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3133\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
